Article 11 (Consultations with Local Governments, etc.) Where deemed necessary for the efficient operation of the Integrated Local Subsidy Management System, the Minister of the Interior and Safety may consult the heads of local governments on the following matters:
1. Matters concerning the sharing of financial burdens related to the Integrated Local Subsidy Management System;
2. Matters concerning technical support and allocation of roles for the operation of the Integrated Local Subsidy Management System;
3. Matters concerning joint use of the Integrated Local Subsidy Management System;
4. Other matters for which the Minister deems consultations with the heads of local governments necessary for the efficient management and operation of the Integrated Local Subsidy Management System.
